---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { articles } from '../data/writing.js';
---
<Base
  title="Raphael Fakhri — Mobile & Full-Stack Software Engineer"
  description="Mobile and full-stack software engineer in Beirut owning React Native/Expo apps, .NET/C# backends, and production AI systems end-to-end."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-top">
      <img
        class="avatar"
        src="/raphael.jpg"
        alt="Portrait of Raphael Fakhri"
        width="88"
        height="88"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <div>
        <h1>Raphael Fakhri</h1>
        <p class="hero-role">Mobile &amp; Full-Stack Software Engineer &middot; Beirut, Lebanon</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="hero-lead">
      I own software end-to-end&mdash;from mobile apps in <strong>React Native (Expo)</strong> and backend systems in <strong>.NET / C#</strong> and <strong>Python</strong> to CI/CD, store releases, and production AI pipelines. I care most about dissecting a problem properly before writing code, finding the real bottleneck, and shipping software that holds up under real users.
    </p>

    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:mail@raphaelfakhri.com">Email me</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/cv/">Read CV</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/raphaelfakhri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>

    <dl class="proof-strip">
      <div>
        <dt>Mobile &amp; Cross-Platform</dt>
        <dd>130+ screen Expo / React Native app shipped to iOS, Android &amp; Web</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Backend &amp; Production AI</dt>
        <dd>.NET 8, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, Python, Temporal &amp; LiveKit</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Upstream Open Source</dt>
        <dd>Merged fixes in Callstack, Software Mansion, FluentMigrator &amp; LiveKit</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="story" class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Story</div>
    <h2>How I got here</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I started building production systems while studying Computer Science at Saint Joseph University in Beirut&mdash;shipping .NET Core and RabbitMQ APIs for a Student Information System alongside an external vendor, redesigning relational schemas to migrate production data from MySQL to PostgreSQL, and delivering a 15+ page HR module with granular SQL permissions.
      </p>
      <p>
        During my MSc in Computer Science at the American University of Beirut (GPA 3.81), I spent two years as the sole developer and designer of AUB Mediterraneo&rsquo;s campus web platform (<a href="https://aubmed.ac.cy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aubmed.ac.cy</a>). Sitting directly with non-technical university staff taught me a lesson that stuck: most engineering waste comes from solving the wrong problem too fast. Turning messy operational goals into clear specs let me ship 200+ change requests with 100% on-time delivery.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since then, I&rsquo;ve worked across enterprise data infrastructure at Cardinal Health | WaveMark (building an autonomous Python/DSPy drift-reconciliation agent across ClickHouse, Kafka, and Elasticsearch), scoped cloud and AI architectures with enterprise technical leads at Nebulane, and taken full sole-engineer ownership of client products&mdash;most notably Zaky, a cross-platform AI tutoring app live on iOS, Android, and Web&mdash;while contributing bug fixes upstream to the open-source libraries I rely on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Selected Work</div>
    <h2>Systems I&rsquo;ve shipped</h2>

    <div class="case-grid">
      <article class="card card-featured">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div>
            <h3>Zaky &mdash; Cross-Platform AI Tutoring App</h3>
            <p class="card-meta">Client work &middot; Sole Engineer &middot; Apr 2026&ndash;Present</p>
          </div>
          <span class="badge">Live on iOS, Android &amp; Web</span>
        </div>

        <div class="case-columns">
          <div>
            <p class="label">The Problem</p>
            <p>
              Build a complete grades 1&ndash;12 tutoring and marketplace app from scratch across three platforms&mdash;combining live 1:1 teacher sessions with an AI pipeline that turns a student&rsquo;s photo of a homework exercise into a mathematically checked explainer video.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="label">What I Built</p>
            <p>
              Architected a 130+ screen Expo SDK 55 / React Native 0.83 TypeScript client (student, teacher, and admin roles) with serialized MMKV-to-server state sync, stale-overwrite guards, offline queues, and zero-data-loss storage migrations. Wrote a native Kotlin Expo module for Android Credential Manager alongside Sign in with Apple, LiveKit WebRTC lessons with shared whiteboard and iOS background audio, AR/EN/FR RTL localization, and automated CI/CD with one-command EAS Update rollback. On the backend, built the Python homework pipeline (vision crop &rarr; Claude &rarr; SymPy verification &rarr; Manim + ElevenLabs narrated video).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Live since October 2026 across iOS, Android, and Web, serving 760+ student requests across 100+ devices with separate dev/prod environments and graceful job-draining releases.
        </p>

        <ul class="tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
          <li>React Native</li>
          <li>Expo SDK 55</li>
          <li>TypeScript</li>
          <li>Kotlin</li>
          <li>MMKV</li>
          <li>LiveKit</li>
          <li>Python</li>
          <li>SymPy &amp; Manim</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div>
            <h3>Upstream Open-Source Contributions</h3>
            <p class="card-meta">React Native &middot; .NET &middot; WebRTC &middot; Temporal</p>
          </div>
          <a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <p>
          When production systems hit framework edge cases, I fix them upstream rather than piling on fragile workarounds. Selected merged PRs reviewed and accepted by core maintainers:
        </p>
        <ul class="pr-list">
          <li>
            <strong>React Native ecosystem:</strong> Fixes across Callstack (Brownfield iOS NSNumber boxing, Re.Pack, Paper, React Native Testing Library), Software Mansion (Gesture Handler, Enriched HTML), RevenueCat, and LiveKit.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>.NET infrastructure:</strong> 10 merged PRs in FluentMigrator&mdash;including <a href="https://github.com/fluentmigrator/fluentmigrator/pull/2384" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">provider-agnostic NULL semantics for unique indexes (#2384)</a> across eight SQL engines and a <a href="https://github.com/fluentmigrator/fluentmigrator/pull/2385" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Roslyn analyzer code fix (#2385)</a>&mdash;plus 10 merged PRs in Swashbuckle.AspNetCore (<a href="https://github.com/domaindrivendev/Swashbuckle.AspNetCore/pull/4128" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#4128</a>, <a href="https://github.com/domaindrivendev/Swashbuckle.AspNetCore/pull/4116" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#4116</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>WebRTC &amp; distributed systems:</strong> RTX payload-type negotiation in <a href="https://github.com/livekit/livekit/pull/5135" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LiveKit SFU (#5135, Go)</a> and <a href="https://github.com/versatica/mediasoup/pull/1953" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">mediasoup (#1953, C++)</a>, <a href="https://github.com/livekit/ingress/pull/554" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WHIP ICE restarts (#554)</a> in LiveKit Ingress, and fixes across Temporal&rsquo;s .NET, Python, TypeScript, and PHP SDKs.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <div class="two-col">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>AUB Mediterraneo Web Platform</h3>
          <p class="card-meta">American University of Beirut &middot; 2023&ndash;2025</p>
          <p>
            Sole engineer and designer for <a href="https://aubmed.ac.cy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aubmed.ac.cy</a> (C#/.NET on SharePoint, 50+ responsive pages, in-page PDF viewer, tree navigation). Turned staff requests into specs and shipped 200+ updates with 100% on-time delivery.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>C# / .NET</li>
            <li>JavaScript</li>
            <li>SharePoint</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Schema &amp; Data-Drift Agent</h3>
          <p class="card-meta">Cardinal Health | WaveMark &middot; 2025</p>
          <p>
            Built an automated Python + DSPy reconciliation agent that detects schema and data drift between staging and production across ClickHouse, Kafka, and Elasticsearch, emitting structured patch proposals for engineer review.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>Python</li>
            <li>DSPy</li>
            <li>ClickHouse</li>
            <li>Kafka</li>
            <li>Elasticsearch</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <h3>shipment-triage</h3>
            <a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri/shipment-triage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code &rarr;</a>
          </div>
          <p class="card-meta">Open-Source Project &middot; Durable Agentic Workflow</p>
          <p>
            Logistics exception-handling workflow on Temporal and LangGraph with Qdrant RAG and a durable human approval gate. CI kills the sole worker mid-activity to assert crash recovery without duplicate writes, gated by DeepEval.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>Temporal</li>
            <li>LangGraph</li>
            <li>Qdrant</li>
            <li>DeepEval</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <h3>grant-management-api</h3>
            <a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri/grant-management-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code &rarr;</a>
          </div>
          <p class="card-meta">Open-Source Project &middot; .NET 8 &amp; SQL Server</p>
          <p>
            Clean-architecture .NET 8 REST API with hand-written T-SQL tuning (filtered covering indexes, views, stored procedures), 70 unit and integration tests, non-root Docker, and Kubernetes Job migrations verified on a live kind cluster in CI.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>.NET 8</li>
            <li>EF Core</li>
            <li>T-SQL</li>
            <li>Docker &amp; K8s</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>24/7 Unified AI Customer Support</h3>
          <p class="card-meta">Client Work &middot; Production Operations</p>
          <p>
            Built and operate a client&rsquo;s end-to-end AI support agent on self-hosted Chatwoot and Claude, unifying web chat, Shopify, WhatsApp, email, and mobile routing&mdash;running continuously in production without incident.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>Chatwoot</li>
            <li>Claude API</li>
            <li>Shopify</li>
            <li>WhatsApp</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <h3>Parallel Heaps in CUDA &amp; MSc Thesis</h3>
            <a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri/Generalized_Heaps_Parallel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code &rarr;</a>
          </div>
          <p class="card-meta">Systems &amp; Research &middot; AUB MSc CS (GPA 3.81)</p>
          <p>
            Implemented block- and warp-level CUDA heap operations with coalesced shared-memory access (88% faster sorting 10M+ elements). MSc thesis: a VS Code extension explaining code in place selected via mouse, voice, or eye-tracker gaze.
          </p>
          <ul class="tags">
            <li>CUDA / C++</li>
            <li>VS Code API</li>
            <li>HCI Study</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="writing" class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Writing</div>
    <h2>Engineering notes</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Short notes from building and debugging real production systems.</p>

    <div class="article-list">
      {articles.map((article) => (
        <a class="article-row" href={`/writing/${article.slug}/`}>
          <div class="article-meta">
            <time datetime={article.isoDate}>{article.date}</time>
            <span>&middot;</span>
            <span>{article.readTime}</span>
          </div>
          <h3>{article.title}</h3>
          <p>{article.summary}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="section">
    <div class="contact-box">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Get in touch</div>
      <h2>Let&rsquo;s build something solid</h2>
      <p>
        If you&rsquo;re hiring a senior mobile or full-stack engineer who owns systems end-to-end&mdash;or scoping a product that needs real engineering rigor&mdash;send me an email directly.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:mail@raphaelfakhri.com">mail@raphaelfakhri.com</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/cv/">View CV</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/raphaelfakhri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/RaphaelFakhri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero-top {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.15rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
    }

    .avatar {
      width: 82px;
      height: 82px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      object-fit: cover;
      border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
      flex-shrink: 0;
      display: block;
    }

    .hero-role {
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-weight: 500;
    }

    .hero-lead {
      font-size: 1.07rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      max-width: 66ch;
      margin-bottom: 1.45rem;
    }

    .hero-lead strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.6rem;
    }

    .btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      font-weight: 550;
      transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .btn:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .btn-primary {
      background: var(--accent);
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: #ffffff;
    }

    .btn-primary:hover {
      background: var(--accent-hover);
      border-color: var(--accent-hover);
      color: #ffffff;
    }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      .btn-primary {
        color: #0b1120;
      }
      .btn-primary:hover {
        color: #0b1120;
      }
    }

    .proof-strip {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.9rem;
      margin: 2rem 0 0;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }

    .proof-strip dt {
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

    .proof-strip dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    .prose p {
      max-width: 68ch;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .case-grid {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1.1rem;
    }

    .two-col {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.1rem;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
    }

    .card-featured {
      border-color: var(--accent-border);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--accent-soft) 0%, var(--surface) 38%);
    }

    .card-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .card-meta {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    }

    .card-head .card-meta {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.73rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border: 1px solid var(--accent-border);
      padding: 0.22rem 0.55rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .card-link {
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .case-columns {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.55fr;
      gap: 1.2rem;
      margin: 0.9rem 0 0.95rem;
    }

    .label {
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    }

    .outcome {
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
      background: var(--surface-subtle);
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 0.95rem;
    }

    .pr-list {
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      padding-left: 1.15rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.94rem;
    }

    .pr-list li {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .pr-list li:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .pr-list strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .tags {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }

    .tags li {
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: var(--tag-bg);
      color: var(--tag-text);
    }

    .section-intro {
      margin-top: -0.45rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    .article-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.8rem;
    }

    .article-row {
      display: block;
      padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .article-row:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .article-row h3 {
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }

    .article-row:hover h3 {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .article-row p {
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
    }

    .article-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.45rem;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }

    .contact-box {
      padding: 1.65rem 1.75rem;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }

    .contact-box p {
      max-width: 60ch;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 680px) {
      .proof-strip,
      .two-col,
      .case-columns {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .card-head {
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.45rem;
      }

      .hero-top {
        align-items: center;
      }

      .avatar {
        width: 68px;
        height: 68px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
